# ClaraCasas — hard rules

- **Do not commit, push, or install packages** unless the user explicitly asks.
- **Primary workspace:** `web/` (Next.js 14, Prisma, Tailwind). Scraper is `scraper/`.
- **Locale:** Spanish-only. Unprefixed URLs. `/en` 301s to Spanish. Use `localePath()` / `opportunitiesPath()` / `listingPath()` / `localeToolPath()` — never hardcode tool paths in footers or nav.
- **SEO:** Zone dossiers and opportunities are indexable; dashboard, explore, estimate, heatmap, analyze-url, price-drops, listing detail are **noindex**.
- **Data:** Listing asking prices only — not appraisals or closed sales. Keep disclaimers.
- **Minimize diff** — match existing patterns; no drive-by refactors.

## Docs (open only when needed)

Do **not** load these by default. Open when the task touches that area:

| Doc | When |
|-----|------|
| [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) | Routing/middleware, deal engine, caching, SEO strategy, env vars |
| [`docs/ROADMAP.md`](../../docs/ROADMAP.md) | Prioritization / marking work done |
| [`docs/EMAIL_OPERATIONS.md`](../../docs/EMAIL_OPERATIONS.md) | Email cron / digests |
| [`web/README.md`](../../web/README.md) | Deal analysis details, analyze-url, amenities |

Session doc updates (rules / AGENTS / roadmap) only when you learned something reusable — keep them short. Do not commit docs unless asked.

## Before finishing (TypeScript changes)

From `web/`: `npm run lint` and `npx tsc --noEmit`. Tell the user what to test (locale, opportunities, analyze-url, email).
